Subject: [PATCH] The starter kit at the site's register, with fifteen claims
 fixed against the code

Same standard as the site rewrite the owner ordered: short sentences,
plain words, the binary in and code out, emulation named and framed
per console rather than promised as one blanket safety net. On
PlayStation a dispatch miss halts loudly on purpose; on the cartridge
toolchains the log file's name varies by repo and is now listed per
repo; on the NES the interpreter fallback is off unless the game was
built with push_all_jsr, which only two published ports set.

Every command and flag re-verified against the frameworks themselves:
--disc probes the disc and extracts the boot EXE, it does not stage a
copy (staging is --stage-disc); build needs --rom as well as --output;
the wizard flags and the enable-ci conflict are in the table; the
generate loop uses your real cue path. The invariant core section now
lists only what actually holds across all eight model ports. Timing
takes the sourced shape: about five minutes of game-specific work on a
mature framework, months in the frameworks and in finishing. A
paste-ready prompt block is in the README, every fact inside it
verified, with the catalogue check first and the stop-and-ask rules
that keep a person in the loop.

