+A static recompiler reads a game's binary. A binary is compiled machine code:
+the numbers the console's processor ran, not readable source. The recompiler
+translates that machine code into source code in an ordinary programming
+language. A normal compiler then builds the result into an application for your
+computer.
 
-## Read this before you start
+The technique does not require any one output language. The projects here emit
+C. What comes out is the game's own logic as code, so the game is the program
+you run.
+
+This is not emulation. An emulator reads the game's instructions and acts them
+out one at a time while you play. A recompiled port did that translation once,
+before you played anything.
