+## When it stops
+
+If the game jumps to an address with no generated function behind it, the
+runtime records the address, dumps a crash report and halts. That is on
+purpose. These ports do carry a small emulator, which the framework calls the
+interpreter. It is reserved for code the game writes into RAM while it runs.
+Interpreting around a gap the analysis left would hide the gap.
+
+So there is no miss log file to read here. Ask the debug server: `ping` returns
+`dispatch_miss_total`, `dispatch_stats` reports hits and misses together, and
+`unknown_dispatch_log` dumps the recent ones. Add what you find to the seeds
+and regenerate.
+
